<%# installed by the poetry `screen-chat` recipe - yours to adapt. The
    screen is the chat block with its two addresses: where a message
    posts and where Stop posts. The block partial is the same source
    `bin/rails g poetry:block chat` copies in. It opens on its sample
    conversation, and on its welcome at ?new: put your own messages in
    the sample's place with
    render partial: "chats/message", collection: @messages
    (with no message yet, the block shows its welcome). %>
<%= render "blocks/chat", url: chat_path, stop_url: stop_chat_path %>
